\title{aapalette: Amino-Acid Colour Palettes for Sequence Visualisation}
\description{
A curated set of amino-acid colour palettes, loaded from a single bundled
JSON source of truth (\code{inst/extdata/aa_palettes.json}) so that the R, Python
and Jalview siblings stay consistent.
}
\details{
Three new palettes come from the AApalette project: \code{hue} (normal vision),
\code{redgreen} (red-green colour-vision deficiency) and \code{tritan} (tritanopia).
Seven attributed community-standard schemes are also provided: \code{clustal},
\code{zappo}, \code{taylor}, \code{lesk}, \code{cinema}, \code{rasmol} and \code{shapely}.
}
\section{Colour-vision caveat}{

No 20-colour palette is safe for all deficiencies at once; for robust figures
pair colour with the residue letter (redundant coding). The \code{min_deltaE}
values reported by \code{\link[=aa_scheme_info]{aa_scheme_info()}} are CIEDE2000 minima.
}

